@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+<p><b>Unifi-Presence NG</b> reports the presence of selected UniFi clients via MQTT
+(topic <code>&lt;topic&gt;/&lt;device name&gt;</code>, JSON with <code>connected</code>, <code>ssid</code>,
+<code>signalDbm</code>, <code>ap</code> …) plus summary values such as “anyone home” and groups.</p>
+<p>Supports UniFi OS consoles (port 443), UniFi OS Server (port 11443) and the classic
+Network Application (port 8443) – including Network 9.x, 10.x and 11.x. No Express server and no Node.js required.</p>
+<p>Recommendation: create a local UniFi user without 2FA (the “View only” role for Network is sufficient).</p>
+<p>Documentation: <a href="https://wiki.loxberry.de/plugins/unifi_presence_ng/start" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LoxBerry wiki</a></p>
